WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(bounce music)

00:00:04.013 --> 00:00:04.846
- I'm Katey.

00:00:04.846 --> 00:00:06.946
I made it, I said it,
I ate it, ya heard me?

00:00:06.946 --> 00:00:09.134
(bounce music)

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:11.494
I am from New Orleans, Louisiana,
and I'm a bounce artist,

00:00:11.494 --> 00:00:15.310
aka The Legendary Katey Red, iconic.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.174
(bounce music)

00:00:17.174 --> 00:00:18.175
I was known to be the first

00:00:18.175 --> 00:00:22.299
transgender/homosexual
rapper, bounce artist.

00:00:22.299 --> 00:00:24.966
(bounce music)

00:00:28.831 --> 00:00:31.057
♪ Bounce bounce, do that,
work work, do that ♪

00:00:31.057 --> 00:00:32.777
- [Narrator] That, is Miss Katey Red.

00:00:32.777 --> 00:00:34.448
A legendary bounce artist who's

00:00:34.448 --> 00:00:37.067
been doing it for over 20 years.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:40.746
But before we get to her
story, what exactly is bounce?

00:00:40.746 --> 00:00:42.465
- People may call it "twerking,"

00:00:42.465 --> 00:00:44.711
the correct name for it is "bouncing."

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.372
It's shake-your-ass music,
that's what bounce music is, it's

00:00:46.372 --> 00:00:47.546
shake-your-ass music.

00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:50.046
(dance music)

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.890
- [Narrator] The origin of
bounce music can be traced back

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.753
to the mid '80s, to a DJ duo from Queens,

00:00:57.753 --> 00:00:59.914
known as The Showboys.

00:00:59.914 --> 00:01:03.072
They took the theme from Dragnet

00:01:03.072 --> 00:01:04.219
and sampled it into this:

00:01:04.219 --> 00:01:06.170
("Drag Rap" by The Showboys)

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:07.909
Eventually, it made its way to New Orleans

00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:09.957
where the beat got sped up, looped,

00:01:09.957 --> 00:01:12.637
and by the early '90s,
bounce was a mainstay

00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:15.014
in New Orleans music.

00:01:15.014 --> 00:01:18.265
Soon enough, bounce went from
a hyperlocal New Orleans sound

00:01:18.265 --> 00:01:20.734
to influencing some of
mainstream's biggest artists,

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.654
like Drake and Beyoncé.

00:01:22.654 --> 00:01:26.349
("Formation" by Beyoncé)

00:01:26.349 --> 00:01:28.896
- [Katey] I don't know what
it is about that sound,

00:01:28.896 --> 00:01:30.294
but whatever that sound be,

00:01:30.294 --> 00:01:32.033
it have you moving to your feet, baby.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:34.533
(dance music)

00:01:37.443 --> 00:01:40.433
My fist concert, I was scared.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.016
I was scared, I was so nervous.

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:47.331
As soon as I got up there, and I was like

00:01:47.331 --> 00:01:48.354
"How y'all doin'?"

00:01:48.354 --> 00:01:49.623
and they was screaming out loud,

00:01:49.623 --> 00:01:50.777
"We love you! We love your music!"

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.683
And I'm like, (sigh of relief),

00:01:52.683 --> 00:01:54.345
that was like, what a big relief.

00:01:54.345 --> 00:01:57.566
Let me hear y'all over here,
"Come on, Katey baby, come on!"

00:01:57.566 --> 00:01:59.825
- [Crowd] Come on, Katey baby, come on!

00:01:59.825 --> 00:02:02.204
(bounce music)

00:02:02.204 --> 00:02:03.098
- [Narrator] It takes a certain amount of

00:02:03.098 --> 00:02:06.030
brashness and bravado to
make it as a bounce artist.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:09.209
Let alone as an openly
gay or transgender one.

00:02:09.209 --> 00:02:11.681
But Katey is not one to
shy away from anything.

00:02:11.681 --> 00:02:14.264
(bounce music)

00:02:18.526 --> 00:02:21.422
- Thank y'all, thank
y'all so much for coming.

00:02:21.422 --> 00:02:24.255
I wish I got more time with y'all.

00:02:25.131 --> 00:02:26.899
Me opening doors for a
lot of bounce artists

00:02:26.899 --> 00:02:29.789
and all the gay artists,
I think about that a lot.

00:02:29.789 --> 00:02:32.040
The bounce scene is more
acceptant, but at first it wasn't.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.000
I was bold and brave, but at
the same time I was scared,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.280
but I still had to do me.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.288
A lot of gay guys would
come up here and say,

00:02:38.288 --> 00:02:39.687
"Katey, you are the reason
I told my mom I was gay,"

00:02:39.687 --> 00:02:41.328
because I was like, I
live in the city of music,

00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:43.898
I make people be who they are,
and who they really wanna be.

00:02:43.898 --> 00:02:48.898
You only get one life, and
nobody can run your life but you.

